## Notes for Maintainers (Release 1.0.7)

- **Never claim “Zero Data Loss”, “100 % Safe”, or “ShellCheck PASS”** unless independently proven in the current release cycle.
- All new features must respect `set -Eeuo pipefail`, proper quoting, trap cleanup, and the secure credential pattern introduced in 1.0.6.
- Destination servers **must** be patched against current critical CVEs (including actively exploited CVE-2026-73570 and prior XSS/SSRF issues) before production cutover.
- Prefer official Zimbra upgrade/rolling guides for 8.8.15/9 → 10.1 when possible; treat Z2Z as the clean-state / cross-OS / legacy-source alternative.
- Keep the existing system-account exclusion, admin lockout guard, and checkpoint/resume design as non-negotiable safety invariants.
